<title>USA: Procter &amp; Gamble files $1.375 bln shelf.</title>
<headline>Procter &amp; Gamble files $1.375 bln shelf.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Procter &amp; Gamble Co filed Thursday with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission to register a shelf offering of up to $1.375 billion in debt securities and warrants.</p>
<p>When combined with previously registered securities, the Cincinnati-based consumer products company's shelf offering totals $2 billion.</p>
<p>Proceeds from the sale will be used for general corporate purposes. No underwriters were named in the shelf offering.</p>
</text>
